        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Gunshots fired in standoff at Philippine Senate over ICC suspect Issued on: 13/05/2026 - 17:10 Gunshots broke out at the Philippine Senate on Wednesday and people ran for cover after a top politician wanted by the International Criminal Court said his arrest was imminent and security forces entered the building. Senator Ronald ​dela Rosa, a former ‌police chief who was the main enforcer of ex-Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte's bloody \"war on drugs\", had earlier urged people to mobilise to prevent his ⁠arrest and handover to the ICC. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more. US intel contradicts claims Iran arsenal weakened, The New York Times report 13/05/2026 Taiwan new key player as Ukraine shifts drone supply chain away from China 13/05/2026 France: Cruise ship locked down over likely stomach flu outbreak 13/05/2026 France Xi-Trump summit: The humble soybean at the heart of a trade dispute between the US and China 13/05/2026 King Charles III lays out UK government agenda as Starmer's job hangs in the balance 13/05/2026 Fabled Argentine city Ushuaia tries to shrug off hantavirus suspicions 13/05/2026 REPLAY: King Charles lays out Starmer's agenda as PM fights for survival 13/05/2026 French woman battling 'severe' hantavirus as outbreak grows to 11 13/05/2026 Sarkozy appeal trial: Prosecution wrapping case ahead of sentencing request 13/05/2026"
